WEBVTT

00:00:00.637 --> 00:00:01.630
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.873 --> 00:00:06.882
In this lesson, we do a manicure, then a pedicure, with regular polish,

00:00:06.832 --> 00:00:07.790
step by step.

00:00:08.218 --> 00:00:09.870
Remember three things throughout:

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:13.489
no cutting living skin, cut toenails straight across,

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:16.750
and everything that touches the client must be clean.

00:00:17.411 --> 00:00:18.033
Hands.

00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:19.233
Step one:

00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:20.273
consultation.

00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:24.113
Wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client.

00:00:24.542 --> 00:00:28.353
Ask which shape and color the client wants, and ask about her health:

00:00:28.411 --> 00:00:30.673
any allergies, any diabetes.

00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:32.913
Look closely at the nails and skin.

00:00:33.313 --> 00:00:36.167
If you see unusual signs, do not do the service,

00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:38.913
as in the lesson on when not to treat a client.

00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:40.272
Step two:

00:00:40.456 --> 00:00:41.872
remove the old polish.

00:00:42.131 --> 00:00:47.000
Press a cotton pad soaked in remover on the nail for a few seconds to soften the polish,

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.752
then wipe in a single direction,

00:00:48.938 --> 00:00:50.272
from the cuticle to the tip.

00:00:50.746 --> 00:00:54.352
Do not rub back and forth, or the polish will smear onto the skin.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.512
For any left in the corners, use a wooden stick wrapped with a little cotton.

00:00:59.166 --> 00:00:59.948
Step three:

00:01:00.278 --> 00:01:02.188
trim if needed, then shape.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:06.286
File in a single direction, from the side towards the center,

00:01:06.236 --> 00:01:08.028
in the shape the client chose.

00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:12.668
For choosing shapes, and filing each one, see the nail shaping lesson.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.112
Step four:

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:15.472
soften the skin.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.912
There are two ways.

00:01:17.204 --> 00:01:21.552
Soak the fingertips in warm water, just briefly, then dry them thoroughly.

00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:23.872
Or use a cuticle softener:

00:01:24.141 --> 00:01:28.142
apply it at the base of the nail, leave it for exactly the time on the product,

00:01:28.092 --> 00:01:28.992
then wipe it off.

00:01:29.565 --> 00:01:32.036
This product softens dead skin very quickly,

00:01:31.986 --> 00:01:34.512
so do not leave it on longer than instructed.

00:01:34.843 --> 00:01:37.392
With regular polish, a quick soak is fine.

00:01:37.633 --> 00:01:41.712
But before gel, we prep dry, as the gel polish lesson explained.

00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:43.246
Step five:

00:01:43.624 --> 00:01:44.846
push back the cuticle.

00:01:45.315 --> 00:01:47.143
Hold the pusher at a low angle,

00:01:47.093 --> 00:01:50.526
and push the skin at the base of the nail back very gently.

00:01:51.115 --> 00:01:54.926
Then remove the thin layer of dead skin still stuck to the nail plate.

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:58.766
The nippers are only for cutting pieces of dead skin that have lifted.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.606
Never cut into the living fold of skin, even if the client asks.

00:02:03.172 --> 00:02:04.126
Step six:

00:02:04.382 --> 00:02:07.341
glide a fine buffer very lightly over the nail,

00:02:07.291 --> 00:02:12.046
just to make the surface even and smooth, so the polish goes on beautifully.

00:02:12.386 --> 00:02:13.726
Do not thin the nail.

00:02:14.114 --> 00:02:15.006
Step seven:

00:02:15.258 --> 00:02:16.366
hand massage.

00:02:16.794 --> 00:02:22.037
Apply a little lotion, and gently massage the back of the hand, each finger,

00:02:21.987 --> 00:02:22.926
and the palm.

00:02:23.266 --> 00:02:25.246
Slowly, and evenly.

00:02:25.907 --> 00:02:26.698
Step eight:

00:02:26.867 --> 00:02:28.138
cleanse the nail plate.

00:02:28.475 --> 00:02:31.898
Lotion and oil left on the nail will stop the polish from sticking.

00:02:32.407 --> 00:02:36.263
Take a lint free wipe with cleanser, and wipe each nail thoroughly,

00:02:36.213 --> 00:02:38.138
including both sides and the tip.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.662
Step nine:

00:02:39.775 --> 00:02:40.462
polish.

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:44.062
A thin base coat, to protect the nail and help the color stick.

00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:46.542
Then two thin coats of color.

00:02:46.963 --> 00:02:48.622
Each coat in three strokes:

00:02:48.794 --> 00:02:50.702
middle, left, right.

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:55.182
Leave a small gap at the cuticle, and sweep lightly over the edge of the tip.

00:02:55.611 --> 00:02:58.542
Wait for the previous coat to set before applying the next.

00:02:58.883 --> 00:03:00.462
Finally, the top coat.

00:03:00.641 --> 00:03:04.952
Regular polish applied thick takes a long time to dry, dents easily,

00:03:04.902 --> 00:03:06.142
and smudges easily.

00:03:06.389 --> 00:03:07.565
If it gets on the skin,

00:03:07.515 --> 00:03:11.822
use a wooden stick wrapped with a little cotton dipped in remover to clean up the edge.

00:03:12.453 --> 00:03:13.340
Step ten:

00:03:13.574 --> 00:03:14.220
drying.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.980
Let the client sit and rest, with her hands still.

00:03:18.547 --> 00:03:22.060
To speed it up, you can put a drop of quick dry on each nail.

00:03:22.417 --> 00:03:23.340
Remind the client:

00:03:23.757 --> 00:03:28.140
the surface dries quickly, but underneath, it stays soft for a few hours.

00:03:28.696 --> 00:03:29.594
Now the feet.

00:03:29.825 --> 00:03:30.634
Step one:

00:03:30.903 --> 00:03:32.154
prepare the foot bath.

00:03:32.555 --> 00:03:36.074
The bath has been cleaned and disinfected after the previous client.

00:03:36.502 --> 00:03:39.754
Put in a new disposable liner, then add warm water.

00:03:40.178 --> 00:03:41.674
Test the water with your wrist:

00:03:41.811 --> 00:03:43.594
pleasantly warm, not hot.

00:03:44.103 --> 00:03:46.644
Pedicure tools come out of a sterilization pouch,

00:03:46.594 --> 00:03:48.474
opened right in front of the client.

00:03:48.997 --> 00:03:52.163
Before soaking, look closely at the feet of the client:

00:03:52.659 --> 00:03:57.178
is the skin between the toes cracked, red, or white and soggy,

00:03:57.128 --> 00:03:59.123
are there wounds or ulcers,

00:03:59.551 --> 00:04:03.123
are the nails thickened, discolored, or growing into the skin?

00:04:03.702 --> 00:04:06.611
If you see these signs, do not work on that area,

00:04:06.561 --> 00:04:10.403
and advise the client to see a doctor, or a foot care specialist.

00:04:11.021 --> 00:04:11.844
Step two:

00:04:12.111 --> 00:04:14.804
soak the feet for a few minutes to soften the skin.

00:04:15.312 --> 00:04:17.124
There is no need for a long soak:

00:04:17.393 --> 00:04:22.244
a long soak makes the skin wrinkled and too soft, and very easy to scratch.

00:04:22.593 --> 00:04:27.044
For clients with diabetes, keep the soak short, and the water only lukewarm.

00:04:27.665 --> 00:04:28.490
Step three:

00:04:28.741 --> 00:04:29.770
cut the toenails.

00:04:30.179 --> 00:04:34.413
Place the clippers straight across the edge of the nail, and cut in small snips,

00:04:34.363 --> 00:04:35.930
not the whole nail in one go.

00:04:36.368 --> 00:04:39.690
Do not cut deep into the corners, and do not dig into them.

00:04:40.041 --> 00:04:43.290
The edge of the nail level with the tip of the toe is just right.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:44.746
Step four:

00:04:44.854 --> 00:04:45.546
file.

00:04:45.814 --> 00:04:48.638
File straight across along the edge of the nail,

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:51.066
then just round the corners very slightly,

00:04:51.176 --> 00:04:52.266
so they are not sharp.

00:04:52.608 --> 00:04:54.506
Do not file down into the corners.

00:04:54.814 --> 00:04:55.786
Step five:

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:59.066
push back the cuticle gently, as with the hands.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:00.826
Only remove dead skin;

00:05:01.014 --> 00:05:02.346
do not cut living skin.

00:05:02.943 --> 00:05:03.873
Step six:

00:05:03.976 --> 00:05:04.833
calluses.

00:05:05.243 --> 00:05:10.353
Use a fine foot file, and glide lightly over the heel and the areas of thick skin.

00:05:10.842 --> 00:05:11.553
Evenly;

00:05:11.739 --> 00:05:14.673
a few passes are enough, just to make the skin smoother.

00:05:15.022 --> 00:05:17.153
No blades, and no rasps.

00:05:17.657 --> 00:05:20.373
If a callus is very thick, or has deep cracks,

00:05:20.323 --> 00:05:23.153
advise the client to see a foot care specialist.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:24.594
Step seven:

00:05:24.911 --> 00:05:29.216
gently rub a salt or sugar scrub over the feet and ankles, then rinse,

00:05:29.166 --> 00:05:30.674
and dry them thoroughly,

00:05:30.783 --> 00:05:32.354
especially between the toes.

00:05:32.735 --> 00:05:33.474
Step eight:

00:05:33.743 --> 00:05:35.314
foot massage with lotion.

00:05:35.495 --> 00:05:38.434
Slowly and evenly, along the sole of the foot.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:39.800
Step nine:

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.440
wipe the lotion and oil off the nail plates.

00:05:42.703 --> 00:05:43.960
Put in toe separators.

00:05:44.229 --> 00:05:49.000
Then base coat, two thin coats of color, and a top coat, just as for the hands.

00:05:49.392 --> 00:05:52.680
Wait until the polish has set before the client puts on her sandals.

00:05:53.292 --> 00:05:54.763
Once the client has gone:

00:05:54.951 --> 00:05:56.843
take out the liner and throw it away.

00:05:57.144 --> 00:06:00.653
Clean the bath, then disinfect it for the full contact time,

00:06:00.603 --> 00:06:02.843
according to the product instructions.

00:06:03.111 --> 00:06:06.283
Files, cotton and disposables are thrown away.

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.827
Nippers and pushers go to be washed, then sterilized,

00:06:09.777 --> 00:06:11.963
as in the lesson on tool processing.

00:06:12.298 --> 00:06:15.083
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
